<title>CANADA: Gulf Canada sees higher '97 EPS, cash flow.</title>
<headline>Gulf Canada sees higher '97 EPS, cash flow.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gulf Canada Resources Ltd Chief Executive J.P. Bryan said on Wednesday that the company would see improved earnings and cash flow this year.</p>
<p>Bryan told the annual meeting that Gulf Canada would earn C$45 million or C$0.07 a share in 1997, up from C$37 million or C$0.03 a share last year.</p>
<p>He added that 1997 cash flow would rise to C$600 million or C$2.20 a share from C$410 million or C$1.72 a share in 1996.</p>
</text>
